  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/11-gymnotiformes-knifefishes-of-the-new-world/eigenmannia_trilineata_en/",
      "html": "<p>Eigenmannia are fantastic aquarium fish that show an incomparable elegance. They show three black longitudinal stripes on a smokey ground.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/11-gymnotiformes-knifefishes-of-the-new-world/eigenmannia_trilineata_en/",
      "html": "<p>Specimens were received from Guyana. E. trilineata is known so far only from the Paraguay-Paraná system (Argentina, Brazil, Paraguay, Uruguay).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/11-gymnotiformes-knifefishes-of-the-new-world/eigenmannia_trilineata_en/",
      "html": "<p>Knife fishes need well structured tanks with a good number of hiding places.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/11-gymnotiformes-knifefishes-of-the-new-world/eigenmannia_trilineata_en/",
      "html": "<p>Feeding them is pretty easy, for the fish accept readily any type of live and frozen food. Many specimens also accept granulates.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/11-gymnotiformes-knifefishes-of-the-new-world/eigenmannia_trilineata_en/",
      "html": "<p>Males can reach about 40 cm in length, which is double as long as females can become. Females also have a much shorter snout.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/11-gymnotiformes-knifefishes-of-the-new-world/eigenmannia_trilineata_en/",
      "html": "<p>Breeding of Eigenmannia is possible if a rainy season is imitated. As soon as the fish are in the right condition, they spawn in the roots of floating plants.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/11-gymnotiformes-knifefishes-of-the-new-world/eigenmannia_trilineata_en/",
      "html": "<p>Eigenmannia: dedication name for Carl H. Eigenmann (1863-1927). trilineata: Latin, means \"with three stripes\".</p>"
    }
  ],
